  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity strengthening to KZN Partners in the response to HIV&amp;AIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Goal:  Strengthened capacity of individuals, households and communities to respond to and mitigate the impact of HIV and AIDS in KZN.
Outcomes:
1. Individual, households and communities/organisations are actively engaged in prevention, care and support and mitigation of HIV and AIDS.
2. Community members and organisations are actively involved in shaping policy and practices to address HIV/AIDS , gender inequality and poverty in KwaZulu Natal
3. Improved capacity of faith-based organisations and faith leaders to spearhead the HIV and poverty response in communities in KwaZulu Natal.
CAFOD Project Outcome: Strengthened capacity of KZN Partners in responding to HIV&amp;ADIS challenges.
CAFOD will support the KZN Partners through the intended and identified programme outcomes, but implementing activities that will ensure that the partners have required capacity to facilitate achievement of the outcomes. CAFOD will facilitate: establishment of the reference group and development of the TORs of the group as well as operationalisation of the TORs, organisation and conducting the identification of capacity needs among partners and the initiation of training required, Donors&#x2019; Round table consultation and discussion with partners, evaluation of the programme, resource mobilisation in consultation and support from the PPSS and the PDFO responsible, networking of partners with other networks in the region and exchange visits to expose partners to other projects in the region, in collaboration with the Reference Group.</narrative>
  </description>
